rge v3 (6.2% WER). Scribe v2 supports word-level timestamps, smart speaker diarization, and processes audio across 99 languages, making it a premium choice for absolute accuracy.Speechmatics provides an alternative heavily optimized for enterprise-scale deployments, boasting a 4.72% WER on the FLEURS benchmark. A distinct advantage of Speechmatics is its explicit training on the diverse variations of Catalan dialects, including Central, Valencian, Balearic, Northwestern, Roussillon, and Algherese, ensuring the application remains accurate regardless of the user's specific regional focus. Speechmatics also guarantees real-time API capabilities with less than one second of latency, which is critical for simulating natural conversational cadences.For applications prioritizing ultra-low latency and live conversational flow, Soniox presents a compelling architecture. Soniox is highly optimized for AI voice agents and features built-in endpoint detection, allowing the system to recognize when the user has finished speaking without relying on fragile silence timers. With transcription costs starting at approximately $0.12 per hour of processed audio, it is highly economical for large-scale deployments. Furthermore, Soniox can handle mid-sentence language switching without requiring stream restarts, which is highly beneficial if a user accidentally interjects a Spanish word while attempting to speak Catalan.Alternatively, the application can circumvent cloud processing entirely by leveraging browser-based edge computing. Whisper Web is an open-source platform that executes OpenAI's Whisper models directly within the user's web browser utilizing WebGPU and WebAssembly. Specialized models, such as whisper-small-ca, have been fine-tuned on the Mozilla Common Voice 13.0 dataset specifically for Catalan, achieving a WER of approximately 10.03%. While this error rate is notably higher than cloud-based enterprise models, executing inference directly on the device guarantees absolute data privacy—as the audio never leaves the user's hardware—and eliminates server latency entirely.Finally, for the most culturally authentic implementation, the application should integrate models developed by Projecte AINA. Promoted and financed by the Generalitat de Catalunya and executed by the Barcelona Supercomputing Center, Projecte AINA develops open-source speech models explicitly dedicated to preserving the Catalan language. They host massive ASR models on the Hugging Face platform, such as the whisper-large-v3-ca-3catparla, which is trained extensively on local audiovisual data. More importantly, for the avatars to speak back to the user, the application must utilize Projecte AINA's Text-to-Speech (TTS) models. Their flagship model, Matxa, is a pioneering achievement, representing the first open-source technological solution that offers high-quality text-to-speech interpretation explicitly trained to reproduce the central, north-western, Balearic, and Valencian dialect variants of Catalan. By integrating Matxa, the platform ensures the dynamic avatars speak with absolute cultural and phonetic authenticity.ASR / STT ProviderReported Accuracy (WER)Core Technological AdvantageArchitectural SuitabilityElevenLabs (Scribe v2)3.1% (FLEURS Benchmark)Unmatched precision and word-level timestamping.Premium tier, required for highly nuanced phonetic grading.Speechmatics4.72% (FLEURS Benchmark)Explicitly trained on 6 major Catalan dialects.Ideal for applications prioritizing regional diversity.SonioxNot explicitly publishedUltra-low latency and automatic turn detection.Best for high-speed conversational AI pacing; highly economical ($0.12/hr).Whisper Web (Local)~10.03% (whisper-small-ca)Zero server costs, executes via WebGPU in browser.Optimal for privacy-focused users or minimum viable products (MVPs).To implement the conversational pipeline, the frontend architecture relies on the HTML5 MediaRecorder API to capture microphone input, chunking the audio stream into